Package: rsageRegression
Title: Regression and Generalised Linear Model Module for R Sage
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("R Sage contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "noreply@rsage.dev")
Description: Fits one outcome with linear regression or a generalised linear
    model (logistic, probit, Poisson, negative binomial, Gamma, quasi
    families) from structured terms and models, so interactions and model
    comparisons never pass through free-text formulas. Reports coefficients
    with confidence intervals, standardised effects, hierarchical term
    tests, fit indices and nested model tests on one fixed sample,
    adjusted means, slopes and contrasts, residual, collinearity,
    influence, dispersion and calibration diagnostics, and stepwise AIC or
    BIC search. Fitting uses 'stats' and 'MASS'; tables use 'parameters'
    and 'performance'; adjusted effects use 'modelbased'.
    analyse() returns an 'rsage' result that prints in the console and
    renders in Quarto documents.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: rsage (>= 0.1.0), parameters, performance, insight, ggplot2, stats, utils
Suggests: MASS, car, modelbased, marginaleffects, detectseparation, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
